      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Multidisciplinary pain management clinics provide the standard of care for the diagnosis, evaluation, and treatment of patients who have chronic pain. Primary care physicians are encouraged to maintain an active role in the care of patients after referral to these pain centers, often for long-term opiate therapy or complex regional pain syndrome. Insights into the role of pain management clinics after referral are discussed in this article."},
